---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const title = "Disclaimer | PVF Calculator";
const description = "Disclaimer for pvfcalculator.com — limitations of calculator accuracy and appropriate use of weight and dimension estimates.";
const canonical = "https://pvfcalculator.com/disclaimer/";
const breadcrumbItems = [
  { name: "Home", url: "/" },
  { name: "Disclaimer", url: "/disclaimer/" },
];
---

<Base title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} breadcrumbItems={breadcrumbItems}>
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden py-16 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <nav class="text-sm text-theme-muted mb-8 flex items-center gap-2">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-theme-primary transition-colors">Home</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <span class="text-theme-primary">Disclaimer</span>
      </nav>

      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-theme-primary mb-2">Disclaimer</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted mb-10">Last updated: September 15, 2026</p>

      <div class="space-y-8 text-theme-secondary leading-relaxed">

        <div class="glass rounded-xl p-5 border border-amber-500/30">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-amber-400 mb-2">Important Notice</p>
          <p class="text-sm">All weights and dimensions provided by PVF Calculator are <strong class="text-theme-primary">theoretical estimates</strong> based on ASME B16.5, ASME B16.9, and ASME B36.10M dimensional tables. They are not certified values and must not be used as the sole basis for safety-critical engineering decisions, lifting and rigging calculations, or pressure system design without independent professional verification.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary mb-3">Calculation Methodology</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">Our calculators use geometric modeling of fitting and flange cross-sections based on dimensional data from the applicable ASME standard editions. Weights are computed as:</p>
          <div class="glass rounded-xl p-4 font-mono text-sm mb-3">
            Weight = Volume × Material Density
          </div>
          <p>Where volume is derived from standard dimensions (OD, bore, wall thickness, hub length, center-to-end distances) and density is selected per the chosen material grade.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary mb-3">Known Limitations and Tolerances</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2">
            <li><strong class="text-theme-primary">Manufacturing tolerances:</strong> ASME standards permit dimensional tolerances on wall thickness, bore, and end preparation. Actual manufactured weights may vary from calculated values by ±3–10%.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-theme-primary">Standard editions:</strong> Dimensional values may differ between editions of a given standard. Our data reflects the editions current at the time of implementation.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-theme-primary">Special specifications:</strong> Customer-specified extra wall, custom bore, or non-standard end preparations are not reflected in standard calculations.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-theme-primary">Forgings and castings:</strong> Forged and cast components may have material distribution that differs from theoretical geometric models.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-theme-primary">Large bore and non-standard sizes:</strong> Accuracy may be reduced for sizes at the extremes of the standard's coverage range.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary mb-3">Appropriate Use Cases</h2>
          <div class="space-y-3">
            <div class="flex gap-3 items-start">
              <span class="text-green-400 font-bold shrink-0 mt-0.5">✓</span>
              <p>Freight cost estimation and container planning for procurement shipments</p>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-3 items-start">
              <span class="text-green-400 font-bold shrink-0 mt-0.5">✓</span>
              <p>BOM weight summaries and budgetary estimates</p>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-3 items-start">
              <span class="text-green-400 font-bold shrink-0 mt-0.5">✓</span>
              <p>Invoice sanity checks against supplier theoretical weight calculations</p>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-3 items-start">
              <span class="text-green-400 font-bold shrink-0 mt-0.5">✓</span>
              <p>Engineering education and reference</p>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-3 items-start">
              <span class="text-red-400 font-bold shrink-0 mt-0.5">✗</span>
              <p>Certified weights for customs declarations requiring scale-verified documentation</p>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-3 items-start">
              <span class="text-red-400 font-bold shrink-0 mt-0.5">✗</span>
              <p>Structural and rigging calculations for safety-critical lifts without supplementary engineer certification</p>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-3 items-start">
              <span class="text-red-400 font-bold shrink-0 mt-0.5">✗</span>
              <p>Pressure system design and pipe stress analysis — these require certified manufacturer data and qualified engineering review</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary mb-3">No Warranty</h2>
          <p>PVF Calculator provides this tool "as is" without warranty of any kind, express or implied. We are not responsible for commercial losses, engineering decisions, or safety incidents arising from reliance on calculated values. Always verify against manufacturer data for critical applications.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary mb-3">Reporting Errors</h2>
          <p>If you find a calculated value that appears to differ significantly from a manufacturer's published dimension or certified weight, we want to know. Please <a href="/request-a-quote/" class="accent-text hover:underline">contact us</a> with the specific NPS, schedule, type, and the reference value you're comparing against, and we will investigate and correct if warranted.</p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
